;
; demand_diff_pub_1 -- THE FLAGSHIP (test-matrix C8, owner-ratified D2.11): the
; R-DIFF differential-PUBLISHED demand answer witness. It is the sole
; pre-cutover oracle for the DRInstance::differential pub arm (P-STORE:
; TableIsDifferential(pub) true) -- the demand ANSWER's own pub table is
; @differential, so a live-demand edge retraction must RETRACT the published
; answer through the @differential output tap.
;
; Shape: a @differential (deletion-capable) input `add_edge`, a monotone single
; hop `edge`, a bound #query `neighbors`, and a @differential published tap
; `nbhd_out` over the demanded closure (G-15: any published output over a
; demanded closure whose fabricated demand message is differential must itself
; be @differential -- Differential.cpp faithfulness). Driven with
; `-demand -demand-retract` (.drflags); the .eqgate sidecar re-drives it nested
; under -demand-instance and referees flat == nested == golden LIVE.
;
; The distinguishing move vs demand_diff_input_1 (which stresses demand-death x
; edge-retract interleavings): here the demand STANDS across the retraction --
; epoch 1 lands edges and probes (standing demand for the probed key), epoch 2
; REMOVES an in-answer edge while that demand is still live, and the published
; answer must SHRINK through the diff pub tap (DiffTable Present(key)==true keeps
; the a2' gate OPEN; the net retraction publishes a -delta). If the retraction
; fails to flow (answer does not shrink) or the diff pub arm is unreachable,
; that is exactly the finding this witness exists to surface.

#message add_edge(u64 From, u64 To) @differential.
#local edge(u64 From, u64 To).
edge(F, T) : add_edge(F, T).
#query neighbors(bound u64 From, free u64 To) : edge(From, To).
#message nbhd_out(u64 From, u64 To) @differential : neighbors(From, To).
